    asm: reject L on CALL
    
    As agreed with hww: CALL puts the address after the loop body in SHADOW, so
    "L CALL f" looks like it repeats the loop after f returns, but the loop ends
    there instead. The assembler now rejects L on CALL with the line number; L
    stays allowed on JMP, RET and HALT (e.g. "L JMP.EQ exit" to leave a loop on a
    condition).
    
    Errors are reported in the second pass only (once), and asm_assemble_file
    returns an empty program when there was one, which the testbench, the
    emulator and the asm CLI (now exit status 1) already treat as a failure.
    
    All .asm files in the repository still assemble, and the RTL and C++ tests
    pass.

